{
 "dur": 73.4,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "How does a hydraulic press",
    "crush almost anything?",
    "Your arm pushes.",
    "The oil multiplies."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 6.52,
   "chunks": [
    "Here's a 20-ton shop press,",
    "taken apart:",
    "frame, hand pump, oil reservoir,",
    "and one big cylinder."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 13.11,
   "chunks": [
    "Lift the handle:",
    "a small piston sucks in oil",
    "through a check valve.",
    "Push down: it's forced out",
    "through a second one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 20.37,
   "chunks": [
    "It can't flow back,",
    "so every stroke stacks more oil",
    "on the big piston:",
    "the ram."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 25.45,
   "chunks": [
    "Pascal's law:",
    "squeeze a trapped liquid,",
    "and the pressure is equal everywhere.",
    "Force is pressure \u00d7 area."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 32.29,
   "chunks": [
    "Pump piston:",
    "7/16 of an inch wide.",
    "Ram: 2\u00bc inches.",
    "26 times the area."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 39.11,
   "chunks": [
    "The handle turns a 90-lb pull",
    "into 1,500 lb",
    "on the small piston:",
    "10,000 psi.",
    "On the ram, 40,000 lb.",
    "Twenty tons."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 49.88,
   "chunks": [
    "The catch?",
    "Each stroke moves the ram",
    "about a millimeter.",
    "You trade distance for force."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 55.22,
   "chunks": [
    "A gauge reads the pressure.",
    "A release valve",
    "lets the oil drain back."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 59.71,
   "chunks": [
    "And a soda can?",
    "It buckles at about 200 lb.",
    "Half a percent",
    "of this press."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 66.52,
   "chunks": [
    "What should we take apart next?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v12",
   "t": 68.61,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "the hydraulic press."
   ]
  }
 ]
}